#: 44dd8c0c72a34d389cbecbfde8c5978a
msgid "Parallel Operator Compiler Segmentation Fault"
msgstr "并行算子编译器段错误"

#: 6bc56bebea834ed7a248f1e90e55c0c0
msgid "Status: Open; root cause not proven"
msgstr ""

#: cb4c50a36e194408b74339a110052119
msgid "Last reviewed: 2026-08-12"
msgstr ""

#: 447edeb80a564258a56329cf776c37a1
msgid "Baseline: `582fc51d`"
msgstr ""

#: 0f05b7e152c84e67a5eed459cb917ed2
msgid "Owner: compiler/executor maintainers"
msgstr ""

#: c69e2e658a384a6c851f176eb88245db
msgid "Workaround: `jt.flags.use_parallel_op_compiler = 0`"
msgstr ""

#: 78ad6624fbc740efab4a8515c7ac0779
msgid ""
"Exit condition: a minimized stress test passes repeatedly with parallel "
"compilation enabled and no deadlock, cache corruption, or material "
"regression"
msgstr ""

#: 64e4c75a13f84b519b0ce78f5e112e54
msgid "Symptom"
msgstr ""

#: 168bbf3be30146bd91c12cfdaacfa870
msgid ""
"Some large model and device-parity workloads can terminate with allocator"
" or segmentation faults while multiple fused operations compile "
"concurrently. The failure is timing-sensitive and may surface after the "
"compilation that damaged state, so the last printed operator is not "
"reliable attribution."
msgstr ""

#: 0b2cd605db544409acf6cabea68374f2
msgid ""
"Serial compilation has been used successfully by dataset, ACL, and parity"
" test paths. This is a containment measure, not evidence that runtime "
"operator execution is defective."
msgstr ""

#: 3a5077f26efb4b45af239c178054c86d
msgid "Current hypothesis"
msgstr ""

#: 872ea0bf7f9e4e3f98eca8eac4277b6d
msgid ""
"The leading hypothesis is a missing synchronization boundary between "
"parallel compiler workers and process-level compilation/cache locking. A "
"worker may observe lock state established by the owning process and "
"incorrectly treat shared compiler or relay state as protected. Concurrent"
" mutation could then surface as heap corruption."
msgstr ""

#: fb669e8f0e36488a976c287fc17c93ba
msgid ""
"This remains a hypothesis. The ownership of relay groups, the exact "
"shared mutable object, and the first invalid access have not been "
"demonstrated with a sanitizer trace. Adding one broad mutex is therefore "
"not an accepted fix: it may deadlock nested compilation, eliminate "
"intended parallelism, or fail to protect multi-process cache access."
msgstr ""

#: c5105433025b46489fa7ee21ac99be85
msgid "Reproduction protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ce9be3e62dc14075aca023399cf7d91c
msgid ""
"Use a dedicated state directory and preserve the exact commit, compiler, "
"device, and environment:"
msgstr ""

#: f634214109414879bdd1bdbfcb8c9137
msgid "Run once with the default parallel compiler setting and once with:"
msgstr ""

#: c5a1be3fec8748c4bd99555b82f41ed1
msgid ""
"Do not run the two variants concurrently or against the same cache. A "
"useful reproduction records whether the cache was cold, worker count, the"
" last completed compile, signal/backtrace, and whether repeated serial "
"runs are clean."
msgstr ""

#: 4b5174342de14b5f97fdfe2c40bdd7b4
msgid "Investigation plan"
msgstr ""

#: fba3906acadc47f3ab8dd5e1c9d12dbc
msgid "Minimize the workload while retaining a cold-cache failure."
msgstr ""

#: 5bf7d72de67d424697233c418f57ff9b
msgid ""
"Instrument compiler task creation, relay-group ownership, cache lock "
"acquisition, and worker completion with stable identifiers."
msgstr ""

#: 604a26fc51674028abeed685a30c61ac
msgid ""
"Run the minimized native compiler path under AddressSanitizer or "
"ThreadSanitizer."
msgstr ""

#: 8f89e2fce2bf4e7c96e7e7b3098be0b2
msgid "Identify the first invalid access or race before changing synchronization."
msgstr ""

#: ddc758c6ce7e43aca3900ed700b57cdb
msgid ""
"Apply the narrowest ownership or locking fix and add a deterministic "
"stress regression."
msgstr ""

#: 2cf57030cadf42fe99190a5c991176e0
msgid "Acceptance gate"
msgstr ""

#: 6fb327f1e7be4e19bbac4ccda47a4b47
msgid "A fix must demonstrate all of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ee97be8d0f0742c497f1192a212af15a
msgid "repeated cold- and warm-cache stress runs no longer crash;"
msgstr ""

#: bed0fff7a48142ac911be134703b867c
msgid "a timeout-backed test shows no deadlock;"
msgstr ""

#: 2b9552232c884a81a69d687d2c157ba2
msgid ""
"two processes using separate and shared cache configurations do not "
"corrupt artifacts;"
msgstr ""

#: b5b16079cd744c218d650930b97cdd79
msgid ""
"parallel compile time does not regress materially against the recorded "
"baseline;"
msgstr ""

#: d95b069a8b28479db276cb630e7f2da6
msgid ""
"compiler, device-parity, and representative model tests pass with "
"parallel compilation restored;"
msgstr ""

#: 51e0975a935b409e916f19489c0e9b55
msgid "the serial workaround and ledger entry are removed in the same change."
msgstr ""

#: 6ad2c75bd32c4923964e7e009e824880
msgid ""
"Until that evidence exists, callers that prioritize deterministic "
"validation may disable the parallel compiler explicitly and should report"
" that choice with their results."
msgstr ""
